# Target modern browsers only — our audience is Estonian schools
# using recent Chrome/Edge/Safari/Firefox.  Dropping IE 11 and
# very old Safari saves ~11 KB of polyfill code (Array.prototype.at,
# flat, flatMap, Object.fromEntries, etc.) per the Lighthouse audit.
#
# We use rolling "last 2 versions" per engine so the build target
# automatically advances.  This is equivalent to Baseline Widely
# Available (~30 months behind latest) and is appropriate for a
# marketing site whose audience runs auto-updating browsers.

last 2 Chrome versions
last 2 Firefox versions
last 2 Safari versions
last 2 Edge versions

# Estonia has negligible legacy browser usage.  We explicitly exclude
# IE 11 and Opera Mini which would otherwise trigger unnecessary
# transpilation of modern ES2022+ features.
not dead
not op_mini all
